    {
      "title": "Disk Stack Mental Model and Checking Space",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Disk Stack Mental Model and Checking Space",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Disk Stack",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Block device",
                    "sub": "/dev/sda, /dev/nvme0n1",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Partition",
                    "sub": "sda1, nvme0n1p1",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Filesystem",
                    "sub": "ext4, xfs",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Mount point",
                    "sub": "a directory",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Disk is ==unusable== until it has a **filesystem** and is **mounted**"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. df vs du",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "df",
                "du"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Reports",
                  "Free space per mounted filesystem",
                  "Space used by files under a path"
                ],
                [
                  "How",
                  "Reads filesystem metadata",
                  "Walks the directory tree"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df -h`: human-readable sizes",
                "`df -hT`: adds the filesystem type",
                "`df -i`: ==inode== usage",
                "{red:Full} with free blocks? Inodes ran out (many tiny files)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Ranking Usage",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "du -sh /var/log",
                "du -h --max-depth=1 /var | sort -h"
              ],
              "note": "one total, then one line per subfolder ranked"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "df and du disagree",
              "text": "A deleted file still held open by a running process keeps its space until the process closes it or restarts. Find it: `lsof +L1`"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Identifying Disks, Partitions and Filesystems",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Identifying Disks, Partitions and Filesystems",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Listing devices",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`lsblk` shows a ==tree==: disk → partitions → mount points",
                "`lsblk -f` adds FSTYPE, LABEL, UUID, MOUNTPOINT",
                "`blkid` prints UUID, LABEL and TYPE of each device",
                "Use ==sudo blkid== for devices it cannot read from cache"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Partition tables",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "MBR",
                "GPT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Disk size",
                  "max 2 TB",
                  "over 2 TB"
                ],
                [
                  "Partitions",
                  "4 primary",
                  "128+"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`fdisk` handles ==both==",
                "`parted` and `gdisk` are common alternatives"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Partition, then format",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "lsblk",
                    "sub": "confirm device",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "sudo fdisk /dev/sdb",
                    "sub": "n new, w write",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdb1",
                    "sub": "or mkfs.xfs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Partitioning does ==not== make a filesystem; you still need `mkfs`",
                "{green:ext4}: shrink and grow",
                "{orange:xfs}: grow only"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "mkfs destroys data",
              "text": "Confirm the device name with `lsblk` first."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Mounting and Unmounting",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Mounting and Unmounting",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Attach a Filesystem",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`mount` ==attaches== a filesystem to a **directory**",
                "The directory ==must exist==",
                "Files already in it are {red:hidden} while mounted",
                "`mount` alone or `findmnt` lists mounts; findmnt shows a tree: source, target, type, options"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sudo mkdir /mnt/data && sudo mount /dev/sdb1 /mnt/data"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Unmount and Busy Targets",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`sudo umount /mnt/data` takes the ==mount point== or the **device**",
                "{red:target is busy}: a process uses it, or your shell is `cd`'d inside"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "umount",
                    "sub": "target is busy",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Find blocker",
                    "sub": "lsof +f -- /mnt/data",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Or fuser",
                    "sub": "fuser -vm /mnt/data",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Last resort",
                    "sub": "umount -l",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Persist and Restrict",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Manual mounts ==vanish on reboot==",
                "`-o ro,noexec` gives read-only or restricted mounts",
                "`mount -a` applies everything in `/etc/fstab`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sudo mount -o ro,noexec /dev/sdb1 /mnt/data",
                "sudo mount -a"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Lazy unmount",
              "text": "`umount -l` detaches now and cleans up later. It hides the problem, so use it as a ==last resort==."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "/etc/fstab and UUIDs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "/etc/fstab and UUIDs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The fstab Line",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`/etc/fstab` lists filesystems to ==mount at boot==",
                "One line per filesystem, ==6 fields== in fixed order"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Field",
                "Meaning",
                "Typical"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "1 device",
                  "what to mount",
                  "`UUID=3f2a-...`"
                ],
                [
                  "2 mount point",
                  "target directory",
                  "`/mnt/data`"
                ],
                [
                  "3 type",
                  "filesystem",
                  "`ext4`"
                ],
                [
                  "4 options",
                  "mount options",
                  "`defaults,nofail`"
                ],
                [
                  "5 dump",
                  "backup flag",
                  "almost always `0`"
                ],
                [
                  "6 fsck pass",
                  "check order",
                  "`1` root, `2` others, `0` skip"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "text",
              "lines": [
                "UUID=3f2a-... /mnt/data ext4 defaults,nofail 0 2"
              ],
              "note": "one complete entry"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. UUID and nofail",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Get the UUID from `lsblk -f` or `sudo blkid`",
                "{red:/dev/sdb1} names can change between boots or when disks are added",
                "{green:UUID} stays with the filesystem, so it is stable",
                "==nofail== lets boot continue if the disk is missing",
                "Bad or absent entry without it → ==emergency mode=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Test Before Reboot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Backup",
                    "note": "copy fstab first",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Edit",
                    "note": "add UUID line",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "mount -a",
                    "note": "errors show now",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "findmnt --verify",
                    "note": "check syntax",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never reboot untested",
              "text": "Run `sudo mount -a` and `findmnt --verify` after every edit; a typo can break boot."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Swap and Finding What Fills a Disk",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Swap and Finding What Fills a Disk",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Swap Basics",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Swap = ==disk space== used as overflow when RAM is full",
                "Check with `swapon --show` and `free -h`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Set Up Swap",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sudo fallocate -l 2G /swapfile",
                "sudo chmod 600 /swapfile",
                "sudo mkswap /swapfile",
                "sudo swapon /swapfile"
              ],
              "note": "swap file setup"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Swap file",
                "Partition"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Format",
                  "`mkswap /swapfile`",
                  "`mkswap /dev/sdb2`"
                ],
                [
                  "Enable",
                  "`swapon /swapfile`",
                  "`swapon /dev/sdb2`"
                ],
                [
                  "fstab",
                  "`/swapfile none swap sw 0 0`",
                  "`UUID=<uuid> none swap sw 0 0`"
                ],
                [
                  "Off",
                  "`swapoff /swapfile`",
                  "`swapoff /dev/sdb2`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Disk Full Workflow",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "df -h",
                    "sub": "find full filesystem",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "du drill",
                    "sub": "biggest folder",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Go deeper",
                    "sub": "one level each time",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "find big files",
                    "sub": "-size +500M",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "du -h --max-depth=1 / 2>/dev/null | sort -h",
                "find / -xdev -type f -size +500M"
              ],
              "note": "drill down, then hunt big files"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Usual culprit",
                "Fix"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`/var/log`",
                  "Rotate; `journalctl --vacuum-size=200M`"
                ],
                [
                  "`/var/lib/docker`",
                  "Docker images and volumes"
                ],
                [
                  "Package caches",
                  "Clear old cached packages"
                ],
                [
                  "Core dumps",
                  "Delete old crash dumps"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Swap file",
              "text": "Run ==chmod 600== on it, or swapon warns about insecure permissions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Disk Commands Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Disk Commands Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Space and Devices",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Command"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Usage and type",
                  "`df -hT`"
                ],
                [
                  "Inodes",
                  "`df -i`"
                ],
                [
                  "One total",
                  "`du -sh <path>`"
                ],
                [
                  "Rank subfolders",
                  "`du -h --max-depth=1 . | sort -h`"
                ],
                [
                  "Tree, UUID, fstype",
                  "`lsblk -f`"
                ],
                [
                  "UUID, LABEL, TYPE",
                  "`sudo blkid`"
                ],
                [
                  "Partition tables",
                  "`sudo fdisk -l`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Prepare and Mount",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "sudo fdisk /dev/sdX   # n, then w",
                "sudo mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdX1",
                "sudo mount /dev/sdX1 /mnt/x",
                "sudo umount /mnt/x",
                "findmnt",
                "fuser -vm /mnt/x   # who blocks umount"
              ],
              "note": "mkfs destroys data: confirm the device with lsblk"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Persist and Swap",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "UUID=<uuid> /mnt/x ext4 defaults,nofail 0 2",
                "/swapfile none swap sw 0 0",
                "sudo mount -a   # test before reboot"
              ],
              "note": "first two lines go in /etc/fstab"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`mkswap` formats, `swapon` enables, `swapoff` disables",
                "`swapon --show` lists active swap"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Disk Full",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "df -h",
                    "sub": "full filesystem",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "du drill-down",
                    "sub": "one level deeper",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "find / -xdev -size +500M",
                    "sub": "big files",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "lsof +L1",
                    "sub": "deleted but open",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "df and du disagree",
              "text": "A ==deleted file still held open== keeps its space. Find it with `lsof +L1`, then restart the process."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`df -h` shows / at 100%, but `du -sh /*` adds up to far less. What is going on?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "A deleted file is still held open by a running process, so its space stays used.",
                "`sudo lsof +L1` lists it. Restart that process to free the space."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`sudo umount /mnt/data` fails with 'target is busy', and nothing else seems to use it. What is the likely cause?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Your own shell is cd'd inside /mnt/data. Move out and retry.",
                "`fuser -vm /mnt/data` shows who else holds it."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`df -h` shows 60% free, yet creating a file fails with 'No space left on device'. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The filesystem ran out of inodes, usually from huge numbers of tiny files.",
                "Confirm with `df -i`: IUse% will be 100%."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
